messages:
sylvia: Heads-up — I'm seeing auth + retry weirdness in the new Next.js slim starter (codename 'llamapaths'). On dev it works, but in the edge SSR example we sporadically get 401s and then no retries from the SDK.

raj: Hmm, do you have a minimal repro? Is it the browser auth token or server-side call?

sylvia: Server-side in Edge runtime. Using the JS SDK (v0.9.1) on edge runtime via Next's edge functions. Root request path: /api/generate -> calls Redwood SDK client. Intermittent 401s after a token refresh.

emma: @sylvia can you paste the fetch code? Edge has weird header forwarding. Also remember we added short-lived tokens for hosted customers, maybe refresh flow isn't wired for edge. :thinking_face: 

sylvia: Paste: ```js
// server-side edge handler
import { createClient } from 'redwood-sdk'

const client = createClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY })

export default async function handler(req) {
  const res = await client.generate({ model: 'gpt-lite', prompt: req.body.prompt })
  return new Response(JSON.stringify(res))
}
```
That's simplified — no explicit refresh logic, relying on SDK. When token expires, SDK should auto-refresh then retry the request, but I'm seeing 401 bubbles up to Next and the response is failed.

matt: Can you add a retry wrapper temporarily? Something like: ```js
async function withRetries(fn) {
  for (let i=0;i<3;i++){
    try { return await fn() } catch(e) {
      if (e.status === 401) { await sleep(200*i); continue }
      throw e
    }
  }
  throw new Error('retries exhausted')
}
```
That can confirm if it's a one-off race on refresh.

raj: Also check that the edge env has access to the KMS or env rotation mechanism. We had a bug where process.env could be stale under edge warm starts.

sylvia: Will try the withRetries hack. Quick note: behavior differs when running locally vs deployed to staging in Vercel Edge — locally it's fine. On staging we see ~2% failed requests over 1k calls.

emma: Could be the SDK's refresh lock not working under multiple concurrent inflight requests in the same lambda-like instance. We added a mutex in node but not in edge runtime.

matt: Ok this is actionable. Proposal: (1) add a lightweight retry + idempotency hint on the sample; (2) file an SDK parity bug to ensure refresh lock works in Web/Eedge runtime; (3) update starter docs to call out recommended practice for short-lived keys in edge.

raj: Agree. For the issue, label it "sdk:edge-refresh" and assign to eng-devex. @emma can you own the SDK fix?

emma: I can take it. I'll add tests simulating concurrent calls in the edge-runtime emulator and roll a patch. ETA EOW.

sylvia: In the starter app I'll add an opt-in env var RW_EDGE_RETRY=true and the temporary withRetries wrapper plus a short blurb in README. PR incoming.

deploy-bot: Deployment started for sylvia/llamapaths-edge-fix (staging) — build 2026.3.12-4821

matt: Nice. Once Emma's patch is in, we should revert the wrapper in the sample to avoid encouraging global retries by default. Instead show a small snippet in README under "Edge best practices".

raj: Also we should add a small e2e test in the sample's CI that spikes concurrent requests to /api/generate and asserts <1% 5xx/401s so we don't regress.

emma: Will add: unit tests + integration in SDK, and a short changelog entry.

sylvia: Thanks team — will send the PR for the starter and link the SDK issue in the thread. If anyone wants to review the sample's README blurb ping me. :raised_hands:
